<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zwide</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1758–1825</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Zwide kaLanga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zwide was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndwandwe">Ndwandwe</a> in present-day northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwazulu-natal">KwaZulu-Natal</a> in the late 18th and early 19th centuries. He killed the Mthethwa leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingiswayo">Dingiswayo</a> in about 1818 and then fought Shaka's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a>, who defeated him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mhlatuze-river">Mhlatuze River</a> in 1819. The break-up of his kingdom sent his commanders, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soshangane">Soshangane</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwangendaba">Zwangendaba</a>, north to found new states.</p></div>
